# #1717 (R-H): `interface ID(IA[int], IA[str])` is the INTRODUCING declaration, so the gate fires
# at ID itself, not only at a class that names ID. Before: SPY0909. After: SPY0607 at ID.
interface IA[T]:
    def get(self) -> T:
        ...

interface ID(IA[int], IA[str]):
    pass

def main():
    pass
